Previous Lessons:
1. Can't use 'open util/seq[Request]' in Alloy 6 → Must define a concrete signature extending Alloy's built-in 'seq[Request]' instead.
2. Can't parameterize sig headers with seq[Type] in Alloy 6 → Must use seq as a field type, not in sig header.
3. Alloy 6 signature field lists must not have a trailing comma before the closing brace—must ensure the brace immediately follows the last field.
4. In Alloy 6, seq[...] is not a built-in type; you must open util/seq before using seq[T] in a field or variable declaration.
5. In Alloy 6, all open statements must be contiguous at the top of the file with no blank lines or comments before them, as their presence will trigger syntax errors.

